 35S     36S(P,D)                      2026JO01                  ENSDF    202509
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35S  c  J|p=0+, T=2 for {+36}S g.s.                                            
 35S  c  2026Jo01: E=66 MeV dispersion-matched proton beam was produced from the
 35S 2c  Separated Sector Cyclotron facility of iThemba LABS, South Africa. The 
 35S 3c  target was 1-mg/cm{+2}, 99.24%-enriched {+36}S powder encapsulated     
 35S 4c  between two 0.5-|mm Mylar foils. The outgoing deuteron and triton      
 35S 5c  reaction products were momentum-analyzed by the K=600                  
 35S 6c  quadrupole-dipole-dipole magnetic spectrometer and detected by the     
 35S 7c  focal-plane detectors consisting of two multiwire drift chambers (MWDC)
 35S 8c  and a downstream plastic scintillator. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced  
 35S 9c  98 levels, L-transfers, and single-neutron spectroscopic factors for 81
 35S Ac  levels from zero-range adiabatic distorted-wave approximation (ADWA)   
 35S Bc  calculations using DWUCK4. Deduced J-dependence of L=2 angular         
 35S Cc  distributions and reproduced with finite-range ADWA calculations.      
 35S Dc  Comparisons with large-scale shell-model and ab initio calculations.   
 35S Ec  Confirmed the N=20 shell closure in {+36}S.                            
 35S  c  Also see Ph.D. Thesis 2021JoZZ.                                        
 35S  cL J,L,S$From ADWA analysis of the measured |s(|q) in 2026Jo01.           
 35S 2cL L-transfers are not specifically given but can be inferred from the    
 35S 3cL reported J|p values. 2026Jo01 selected some J=L-1/2 or L+1/2 based on  
 35S 4cL the observed J-dependence of L=2 angular distributions and based on    
 35S 5cL known J|p values (2011Ch48). When considered in the Adopted Levels,    
 35S 6cL J=L-1/2 or L+1/2 is both allowed unless other constraints are          
 35S 7cL available.                                                             
 35S  cL S$C{+2}S from 2026Jo01. For levels with J|p=(1/2-,3/2-), the C{+2}S    
 35S 2cL values are given for 3/2-. C{+2}S is normalized to a {+40}Ca benchmark 
 35S 3cL where Woods-Saxon parameters (r{-0}=1.27 fm, a{-0}=0.70 fm) were       
 35S 4cL adjusted to ensure the summed strength of the 1d{-3/2}, 2s{-1/2}, and  
 35S 5cL 1f{-7/2} orbitals equals 6. A systematic uncertainty of 11.2% is       
 35S 6cL associated with all spectroscopic factors due to the effective         
 35S 7cL target-thickness variation (10%) and the nominal target thickness      
 35S 8cL uncertainty (5%) (2026Jo01). This uncertainty is included by the       
 35S 9cL evaluators.                                                            
 35S  cL ISPIN$T=3/2 or 5/2 for {+35}S levels populated in the {+36}S(p,d)      
 35S 2cL reaction based on T=2 for the 0+ g.s. of {+36}S. {+35}S levels below 9 
 35S 3cL MeV are likely T=3/2 and those above 9 MeV are likely T=5/2 considering
 35S 4cL the binding, Coulomb, and proton-neutron mass differences suggest the  
 35S 5cL IAS of {+35}P ground state (T=5/2) should be around 9017 keV in {+35}S.
 35S 6cL C{+2}S extracted for these {+35}S levels show excellent agreement with 
 35S 7cL proton-removal data from {+35}P when scaled by expected Clebsch-Gordan 
 35S 8cL ratio of 0.167 (2026Jo01).                                             
